# `sum()` stores on what `base()` has from one of the closures that lie under `createBase`, and each of them that constructs anything constructs `Made`, one through `counted()`, which returns its argument as it came.
# So the image has the order `kind pos flags | left right note` for the member of `Made` with the tag 1, and none for that of `Small`. The records are those of answers/factory-fills-a-member-of-a-tagged-family.ir,
# with what is written of the three objects (`as Sum`: L2, `as Leaf`: L3, `as Name`: L6) laid into the conversions, and `Any` (L2|L3|L6) into the fields `left` and `right` of `Sum`, BY HAND: the tool that makes a test from a source leaves the interfaces out of the types. A store tests what is stored against the field's written type: left as `undefined|null`, that test can only pass while nothing is known of `sum`'s parameters, and they are proven objects.
